{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_642","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H10 — Configuration resolver: selective recovery policy\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Error-handling evolution (2/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic configuration resolver\n(single module `h10.profile`). Profiles have an id, a value, and a state\n(`ok` / `malformed` / `internal`). `resolve_value(profiles, key)` returns the\nvalue of an `ok` profile. The result type is already `result string string`;\n**do not change any return type**. The current policy is coarse: **every**\nnon-ok outcome silently recovers to the deterministic default `\"unknown\"` —\nincluding malformed and internal failures.\n\nThe program is driven by the environment variable `H10_SCENARIO` and prints\ndeterministic lines.\n\n## Required change\n\nIntroduce a **selective recovery policy**:\n\n```text\nmissing key             -> recover with the deterministic default \"unknown\"\nmalformed value         -> propagate  E_H10_INVALID: <key>\ninternal failure        -> propagate  E_H10_INTERNAL: <key>\n```\n\nRequirements:\n\n- the default fallback may be used **only** for a missing key;\n- malformed / invalid values must **not** silently fall back;\n- internal failures must **not** be masked by the default;\n- success inputs must keep the real value (must not always return the\n  default);\n- a recovered result is observable: it returns exactly `\"unknown\"` (the\n  deterministic default), distinguishable from any real profile value.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier drives the compiled program through scenarios and checks\nexact output lines: success value, missing-key recovery, malformed\npropagation, internal propagation, and the absence of silent fallback on\nnon-missing failures.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
